<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sea Beggars</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Watergeuzen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sea Beggars (Watergeuzen) were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Protestant privateers who fought Spanish rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> from 1568, sailing under letters of marque from William of Orange. Expelled from English ports, they captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brielle">Brielle</a> on 1 April 1572 and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlissingen">Flushing</a>, setting off revolts across Holland and Zeeland that made the two provinces the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sea-beggars.jpg" alt="Sea Beggars" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hendrick Cornelisz Vroom · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vroom_Hendrick_Cornelisz_Battle_of_Haarlemmermeer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
